---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'

const shipped = [
  ['Auth & ledger', 'Users, accounts, categories, rules, transactions and splits — all under row-level security. Account balances are derived from the ledger, never stored.'],
  ['App shell & plugin host', 'Module Federation host with dashboard widgets contributed by plugins, and per-plugin database roles derived from each plugin’s manifest.'],
  ['Import & categorization', 'CSV import with saved column mappings, duplicate detection and batch undo. Category rules with a preview, plus triage on the Transactions page.'],
  ['Self-hosting release (v0.1.0)', 'A self-hosting quickstart, a published container image, the plugin SDK and UI kit on npm, and a light/dark/system theme switch.'],
  ['Recurring items & Until payday (v0.2.0)', 'A Recurring page for income, bills, debt payments and transfers, with split paychecks as one item. The Until payday widget shows what’s safe to spend before your next paycheck and warns, per account, before a balance drops below its buffer.'],
  ['Forecast & time zone (v0.2.1)', 'A Forecast page projecting one account’s daily balance from its recurring items, out to 90 days, 6 months or the end of the year. “Today” follows your own time zone.'],
  ['Paid / landed matching (v0.3.0, v0.4.0)', 'Match a transaction to the recurring item it paid, from the Recurring page or the Transactions page, so nothing is counted twice. Skip, move or change one occurrence, see late payments flagged, and dismiss a wrong suggestion with “Not this”.'],
  ['Budgets plugin', 'Per-category monthly budgets with per-line rollover, plus budget windows (v0.3.0): one amount for one category across a date range, like holiday gifts.'],
  ['Plugin manager & roles (v0.4.0)', 'The instance’s owner turns plugins on and off from Settings, applied live, with each plugin’s data kept while it’s off. The first account is the owner; later sign-ups are members.'],
  ['Errors on the field (v0.4.0)', 'Every form checks what it can before sending and shows each problem under the field it’s about.'],
  ['Starter categories (v0.4.1)', 'Memberships and Domains / web hosting join the starter set; “Run setup again” adds them to an account that’s already set up.'],
  ['Phones & accessibility (v0.4.2)', 'A navigation drawer and card layouts on small screens, collapsible Categories and Rules, icon row actions, a skip link and a title for every page.'],
]

const now = [
  'A screen for owners to change another account’s role, instead of SQL.',
  'A layout pass on the Transactions table, which is crowded since the Recurring column was added.',
  'A settings danger zone with two separately-confirmed actions: “erase my data” (your own rows across core and every plugin) and, for an owner, “erase this entire instance”.',
]

const next = [
  'A debt payoff plugin (snowball and avalanche), keeping its own per-debt balance, rate and minimum payment.',
  'A per-plugin theme contribution point, so a plugin can ship an additional theme alongside the built-in light/dark/system switcher.',
]

const later = [
  'Cross-plugin data access — a plugin reading data another plugin owns, such as debt details feeding net worth or FIRE, or comparing two budgeting plugins side by side. Today a plugin only sees core tables.',
  'An envelope budgeting plugin alongside the existing budgets plugin.',
  'FIRE plugins (lean, fat, barista, coast), comparable side by side on a shared calculation module and light enough to run several at once.',
  'Extending the shortfall warning to savings and other accounts, measured against each account’s buffer amount, for planning larger purchases.',
  'Editing an occurrence from the calendar widget, and a month grid view.',
  'Suggesting recurring items by detecting patterns in your transaction history.',
  'Themes as a data-only plugin type: a validated set of design tokens, no code.',
  'Third-party plugin installation — blocked on plugin isolation, which doesn’t exist yet; all plugin code today runs fully trusted.',
  'Freezing the plugin API (SDK_MAJOR_VERSION) ahead of 1.0.',
]
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Features"
  description="What Wicker Money does today, what's being built now and what's next, taken straight from the project's roadmap rather than marketing copy."
>
  <section class="wmm-section wmm-page-hero">
    <div class="wmm-container">
      <p class="wmm-eyebrow">Shipped vs. planned</p>
      <h1>What's built, and what isn't yet</h1>
      <p class="wmm-lede">
        Wicker Money is pre-1.0 with a single maintainer. This page mirrors
        <a href="https://github.com/wickermoney/wicker-money/blob/main/ROADMAP.md">the project's ROADMAP.md</a>
        directly rather than restating it loosely, so it can't drift into overpromising.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wmm-section wmm-section--alt">
    <div class="wmm-container">
      <h2><span class="wmm-status-badge wmm-status-badge--shipped">Shipped</span> Through v0.4.2</h2>
      <table>
        <tbody>
          {shipped.map(([name, note]) => (
            <tr>
              <td style="width: 220px; font-weight: 600;">{name}</td>
              <td>{note}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p class="wmm-fineprint">Two more bundled plugins, insights and spending-trends, also ship in the image — see the repo for what they currently cover.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wmm-section">
    <div class="wmm-container wmm-roadmap-grid">
      <div>
        <h2><span class="wmm-status-badge wmm-status-badge--now">Now</span> Polish after the plugin manager</h2>
        <ul>
          {now.map((item) => <li>{item}</li>)}
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2><span class="wmm-status-badge wmm-status-badge--next">Next</span></h2>
        <ul>
          {next.map((item) => <li>{item}</li>)}
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wmm-section wmm-section--alt">
    <div class="wmm-container">
      <h2><span class="wmm-status-badge wmm-status-badge--later">Later</span></h2>
      <ul class="wmm-later-list">
        {later.map((item) => <li>{item}</li>)}
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wmm-section">
    <div class="wmm-container">
      <h2>How the plugin model works</h2>
      <p class="wmm-lede" style="max-width: 72ch;">
        The core owns identity, money movement and the app shell. Everything that
        <em>interprets</em> money &mdash; budgets, forecasting, FIRE, importers
        &mdash; is a plugin built against <code>@wickermoney/plugin-sdk</code>. A fresh
        install is useful on its own; bundled plugins hold no privileges a third-party
        plugin couldn't also request. The instance's owner can turn any plugin on or
        off from Settings, and a plugin that's off keeps its data until it's turned
        back on.
      </p>
      <p class="wmm-lede" style="max-width: 72ch;">
        The app and bundled plugins are AGPL-3.0. <code>plugin-sdk</code> and
        <code>ui-kit</code> &mdash; the surface a plugin is built against &mdash; are
        Apache-2.0, which is what makes an independently-built, non-bundled plugin
        licensable on its own terms. Third-party plugin installation itself isn't built
        yet, since it depends on plugin isolation that doesn't exist today.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <style>
    .wmm-roadmap-grid {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
      gap: 48px;
    }
    .wmm-roadmap-grid ul,
    .wmm-later-list {
      padding-left: 20px;
      color: var(--wm-text-muted);
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 10px;
    }
    .wmm-fineprint {
      margin-top: 16px;
      font-size: 0.875rem;
      color: var(--wm-text-muted);
    }
    h2 .wmm-status-badge {
      vertical-align: middle;
      margin-right: 8px;
    }
    @media (max-width: 800px) {
      .wmm-roadmap-grid {
        grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      }
    }
  </style>
</BaseLayout>
